      "sourceTextSha256": "af287bb820439f99a45fd6a6bf294051724f802b5070a114df3034a9cef06dbd",
      "text": "Day 4 · Baños, at about 1,800 m in a lush valley at the foot of Tungurahua Volcano (about 5,020 m), is known for its waterfalls, hot springs and outdoor activities. After a walk through the town centre, follow the Route of the Waterfalls: Agoyán, the Manto de la Novia (Bride’s Veil, with an optional cable car) and the spectacular Pailón del Diablo (Devil’s Cauldron); try the “Swing at the End of the World” or zip-line over the Pastaza Canyon (optional, USD 15). In the evening, return to Quito (about 3.5 hours). Overnight at Hotel Finlandia 4★. (B)",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
